Source: @SOURCE@
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake (>= 3.14)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools

Package: libpio0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Library for accessing Raspberry Pi 5 PIO hardware (fpgas.online build)
 A user-space API to the rp1-pio driver for the PIO hardware of the
 Raspberry Pi 5, cloning the Pico SDK PIO API. This is the fpgas.online
 build of the piolib/ directory of @UPSTREAM_URL@
 @UPSTREAM_REF@ (commit @UPSTREAM_COMMIT@).
 .
 Raspberry Pi's own archive ships libpio0 for the suites Raspberry Pi OS
 is built on; the fpgas.online-fpga-tools apt repository publishes this
 build only for the suites it does not cover, so librp1jtag0 can be
 installed there too.

Package: libpio-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libpio0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Library for accessing Raspberry Pi 5 PIO hardware (development files)
 A user-space API to the rp1-pio driver for the PIO hardware of the
 Raspberry Pi 5, cloning the Pico SDK PIO API.
 .
 This package contains the headers (under /usr/include/piolib) and the
 linker symlink needed to build against libpio0.
